","evidence":["No compose file or devcontainer (docbook/Dockerfile only builds docs with Publican)","No dev/start target","CI starts the app with `php -S localhost:8080` and installs via build/ci_install_mantis.sh"],"gap":"No one-command local environment with a database and seed data.","plan":"Add compose.yaml with MySQL (and optionally PostgreSQL) using the CI values (DB bugtracker, user root/root, port mapping). Add composer scripts `dev` (php -S localhost:8080) and `setup` (composer install, npm ci, install hooks, run the installer and seed via build/ci_install_mantis.sh + build/ci_post_install.sh with local env vars, which also writes tests/bootstrap.php). Write docs/local-dev.md: prerequisites (PHP 8.1+ with mysqli/pgsql, mbstring, curl, gd, soap, ldap extensions; Composer; Node; Docker), first run, reset (drop DB, delete config/config_inc.php), debugging (log_level/log_destination, MANTIS_TESTSUITE_XDEBUG_SESSION)."},{"id":"env-example","status":"fail","evidence":["No .env.example; configuration is PHP: config/config_inc.php.sample lists DB, crypto_master_salt, SMTP and email settings with empty or placeholder values","config/ is gitignored, no .env tracked","CI uses env vars HOSTNAME, PORT, DB_NAME, DB_USER, DB_PASSWORD, DB_HOST, DB_TYPE in build/ci_*.sh"],"gap":"The app reads config from PHP files, not env vars; the CI/local install scripts read env vars that are not documented in an example file.","plan":"Add .env.example listing the variables used by build/ci_install_mantis.sh, build/ci_post_install.sh and compose.yaml (HOSTNAME, PORT, DB_TYPE, DB_HOST, DB_NAME, DB_USER, DB_PASSWORD) with safe local values and a comment pointing to config/config_inc.php.sample for application settings. Do not convert the app to env-based config."},{"id":"toolchain-pinned","status":"fail","evidence":["composer.json: require php ^8.1 and config.platform.php 8.1.34 (not counted by the check)","No .nvmrc / .tool-versions / package.json engines","CI matrix tests PHP 8.1 to 8.5; documentation workflow uses runner default Node"],"gap":"Node version is not pinned and no version file exists for PHP.","plan":"Add .tool-versions (or mise.toml) with php 8.1 (the composer platform floor) and node 20, and add `\"engines\": {\"node\": \">=20\"}` to package.json. Do not change composer platform settings."},{"id":"deploy-explicit","status":"partial","evidence":["docbook/Dockerfile builds documentation only, not the application","build/README.md: release process (tag release-x.y.z, buildrelease-repo.py) for tarballs","README.md: install/upgrade by extracting the tarball and running admin/install.php"],"gap":"MantisBT is a distributed product; how releases are published and how mantisbt.org's own instance is deployed is not written in one place.","plan":"Create docs/deploy.md: sections for release build (build/README.md steps, buildrelease-repo.py), installation/upgrade by users (README.md, admin/install.php), branches master and master-X.Y, rollback (restore backup per README), and uw-harness TODO blocks for who can tag and sign releases, where tarballs are published, and how the project's own tracker is upgraded."},{"id":"observability","status":"fail","evidence":["core/logging_api.php: log_event with log_level (default LOG_NONE) and log_destination (file, page, etc.) from config_defaults_inc.php","api/rest/index.php: unhandled errors written with error_log()","admin/check/index.php: environment checks; admin/email_queue.php shows queued emails"],"gap":"No document on logs, errors or health checks.","plan":"Create docs/observability.md describing log_level/log_destination, PHP error_log for REST errors, show_detailed_errors, admin/check as a health check, email queue monitoring, and TODO blocks for where production logs/alerts live for any instance the team runs."},{"id":"skills","status":"fail","evidence":["No .agents/skills/ or .claude/skills/"],"gap":"No playbooks.","plan":"Create .agents/skills/implement-change, debug-local and rest-api-change (edit api/rest/restcore + core/commands + mantisbt_openapi.yaml, then npm run api:validate and the rest test suite), plus add-language-string (lang/strings_english.txt only; other languages come from translatewiki.net). Symlink .claude/skills to .agents/skills. Any deploy skill must link to docs/deploy.md TODOs."}],"questions":[{"requirement":"deploy-explicit","question":"Who can tag and sign a MantisBT release, and where are release tarballs published (SourceForge, GitHub releases, mantisbt.org)?","why":"build/README.md shows the tagging and build commands but not the publishing target or the people allowed to do it."},{"requirement":"deploy-explicit","question":"Is the project's own tracker at mantisbt.org/bugs deployed from this repository, and if so how and by whom is it upgraded?","why":"Nothing in the repository describes a running production instance of this code."},{"requirement":"observability","question":"For any instance the team operates (for example mantisbt.org/bugs), where are PHP error logs and MantisBT logs stored, and is there any alerting?","why":"The code only exposes log_level/log_destination and error_log; locations and alerts are not visible."},{"requirement":"fast-gate","question":"Is it acceptable that the fast gate needs a local database (Docker compose with MySQL), or do you want a separate DB-free unit suite added for the pre-push gate?","why":"Every existing PHPUnit test boots core.php and connects to a database."},{"requirement":"ci","question":"May the harness change .github/workflows/mantisbt.yml to call a composer gate script, or must CI stay as is and only a new workflow be added?","why":"The existing CI is a tuned PHP x DB matrix maintained by the core team."},{"requirement":"agreements","question":"What is the team's definition of done for a pull request beyond CONTRIBUTING.md (passing CI matrix, reviewer count, who merges, rebase or merge commit)?","why":"CONTRIBUTING.md states targeting and rebasing rules but not review or merge rules."},{"requirement":"local-env","question":"Which database should be the default for local development and the harness: MySQL/MariaDB or PostgreSQL?","why":"CI tests both; the default in config_defaults_inc.php is mysqli."}],"risks":["All PHPUnit suites are integration tests: tests/TestConfig.php require_mantis_core() loads core.php, which needs config/config_inc.php and a database; soap and rest suites also need a running web server and an API token (created by tests/ci_create_api_token.php). A naive `vendor/bin/phpunit` on a fresh clone will fail, so the gates will look broken unless setup installs MantisBT first.","phpunit.xml uses bootstrap=tests/bootstrap.php, which is not tracked (only bootstrap.php.sample); build/ci_post_install.sh appends to it. Setup must create it.","phpunit.xml sets failOnAllIssues=true: any PHP deprecation or warning (for example on newer PHP versions) fails the run.","build/check_lineterm.php rewrites files when run with options; do not use it as a read-only lint.","No PHP linter or static analyser is configured (no phpcs, phpstan, php-cs-fixer); a lint gate must be added from scratch (php -l is the safe minimum).","Very large legacy procedural codebase (82 entries in core/, ~200 root PHP pages, global $g_ variables) with 15,000+ commits; changes can have wide side effects not covered by tests.","dapphp/securimage is pulled from a VCS repository (github.com/mantisbt/securimage, no-api), so composer install needs network access to GitHub.","Localisation files in lang/ (except English) are overwritten by translatewiki.net commits; agents editing them directly will have changes lost.","admin/ is meant to be removed on live sites; harness scripts must not assume it is reachable in production.","CI is skipped on commits containing '[skip ci]' (translatewiki commits), so those changes are never tested."],"notes_for_apply":"Runtime: PHP 8.1+ (composer platform pinned to 8.1.34; CI tests 8.1-8.5, 8.6 experimental) with extensions mysqli, pgsql, mbstring, json, tokenizer, curl, gd, fileinfo, ldap, soap, zlib (from mantisbt.yml), plus ext-zip for dev. Node 20 for package.json tooling (npm ci). Install with `composer install` (needs GitHub access for dapphp/securimage) and `npm ci`.\n\nReuse composer.json as the PHP task runner by adding a `scripts` section (setup, dev, test, lint, check-fast, check); keep the existing npm api:* scripts untouched. No Makefile exists; do not add one unless composer scripts prove insufficient.\n\nTo run tests locally, mirror CI: start a DB (add compose.yaml with MySQL root/root, database bugtracker), run `php -S localhost:8080` from the repo root, `chmod 777 config/`, then run build/ci_install_mantis.sh and build/ci_post_install.sh with HOSTNAME, PORT, DB_TYPE, DB_HOST, DB_NAME, DB_USER, DB_PASSWORD exported and DB_CMD set (the CI step defines DB_CMD; local scripts must set it too, e.g. `mysql -h127.0.0.1 -uroot -proot bugtracker -e`). ci_post_install.sh uses `sudo chmod` and appends to tests/bootstrap.php and config/config_inc.php, so it is not idempotent: a reset must drop the DB and delete those two files. Prefer a new wrapper script under build/ rather than editing the CI scripts.\n\nNo test is known to be broken on the current code (CI badge on master), but none can run without the installed instance. Suites: mantis, soap, rest, 'mantis core formatting' (use `--testsuite mantis` for a quicker run). failOnAllIssues=true makes deprecations fatal.\n\nDo not touch: vendor/ (composer), lang/ files other than strings_english.txt (translatewiki.net), config_defaults_inc.php semantics, the CI matrix behaviour, docbook build. Do not run build/check_lineterm.php in a gate (it rewrites files). Commit style: short imperative subject lines ('Fix tag cache invalidation', 'Test ... ', 'GHA: ...'); PRs target master and must reference a mantisbt.org issue. Writing rules for prose: no em-dashes, simple English, no hard-wrapping."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2387,"cache_read_input_tokens":60719,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2387},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c229b40-d42e-4c49-9237-42bf46cfedc4","uuid":"9443e99a-7165-446c-aa01-b7f326b73c0f","timestamp":"2026-11-01T18:51:06.733Z","request_id":"req_011Cgci5oWLKxhCPHDkXp48E","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Lez7HZ3LmAmUEfbpniT6oy":{"project":{"name":"MantisBT (Mantis Bug Tracker)","one_liner":"A self-hosted, open-source web bug tracker written in PHP, with a web UI, a REST API, a legacy SOAP API and a plugin system.","value_proposition":"MantisBT lets software teams report, triage, assign and follow issues across many projects from a browser, with configurable workflows, access levels, custom fields and email notifications. Organisations install it on their own web server and database, so they keep control of their data. Integrators automate it through a REST API (OpenAPI-described) and a SOAP API, and extend it with plugins.","users":["Reporter (end user or customer who files issues)","Developer (works on, updates and resolves issues)","Manager (manages projects, versions, categories and users within a project)","Administrator (installs, upgrades and configures the instance, manages users, plugins and workflow)","Anonymous viewer (read-only access when anonymous login is enabled)","API integrator (scripts and tools using the REST or SOAP API with API tokens)","Plugin developer (extends MantisBT through events and the plugin API)"],"use_cases":[{"name":"Report an issue","description":"A user fills the report form (project, category, severity, description, attachments, custom fields) and the issue is created, with notifications sent.","entry_points":["bug_report_page.php","bug_report.php","core/commands/IssueAddCommand.php","api/rest/restcore/issues_rest.php"]},{"name":"View, filter and search issues","description":"Users list issues with saved or ad-hoc filters, view issue details, history and relationships, and export them.","entry_points":["view_all_bug_page.php","view_all_set.php","bug_view_page.php","core/filter_api.php","core/classes/BugFilterQuery.class.php","csv_export.php","excel_xml_export.php","api/rest/restcore/filters_rest.php"]},{"name":"Update and resolve issues","description":"Developers change status, assignee, fields and versions, add notes (bugnotes), monitor, tag, relate and move issues; bulk actions are available.","entry_points":["bug_update_page.php","bug_update.php","bug_change_status_page.php","bugnote_add.php","bug_actiongroup.php","core/commands/IssueNoteAddCommand.php","core/commands/IssueMoveCommand.php","core/workflow_api.php"]},{"name":"Manage projects, versions, categories and custom fields","description":"Managers create projects and subprojects, versions, categories, custom fields and project membership.","entry_points":["manage_proj_page.php","manage_proj_create.php","manage_proj_ver_add.php","manage_proj_cat_add.php","manage_custom_field_page.php","core/project_api.php","api/rest/restcore/projects_rest.php"]},{"name":"Manage users, accounts and API tokens","description":"Administrators create, edit, impersonate and prune users; users manage their own account, preferences and API tokens.","entry_points":["manage_user_page.php","manage_user_create.php","account_page.php","account_prefs_page.php","api_tokens_page.php","core/user_api.php","core/api_token_api.php","api/rest/restcore/users_rest.php"]},{"name":"Configure workflow, thresholds and email notifications","description":"Administrators set status workflow, access thresholds, email notification rules and other configuration stored in the database or config files.","entry_points":["manage_config_workflow_page.php","manage_config_work_threshold_page.php","manage_config_email_page.php","adm_config_page.php","config_defaults_inc.php","core/config_api.php","api/rest/restcore/config_rest.php"]},{"name":"Install and upgrade the instance","description":"The web installer checks the environment, creates or upgrades the database schema and writes config_inc.php.","entry_points":["admin/check/index.php","admin/install.php","admin/schema.php","admin/upgrade_unattended.php"]},{"name":"Integrate through the REST and SOAP APIs","description":"External tools create and read issues, projects, users, filters and config through a Slim-based REST API or the SOAP MantisConnect API.","entry_points":["api/rest/index.php","api/rest/mantisbt_openapi.yaml","api/soap/mantisconnect.php","api/soap/mantisconnect.wsdl"]},{"name":"Roadmap, changelog, summary and news","description":"Users see per-version roadmap and changelog, statistics summary, timeline, news and RSS feeds.","entry_points":["roadmap_page.php","changelog_page.php","summary_page.php","my_view_page.php","news_list_page.php","issues_rss.php","news_rss.php"]},{"name":"Extend with plugins and scheduled tasks","description":"Plugins hook into events (formatting, graphs, avatars, XML import/export); a CLI cron script signals EVENT_CRONJOB and another sends queued emails.","entry_points":["plugins/","core/plugin_api.php","core/events_inc.php","manage_plugin_page.php","scripts/cronjob.php","scripts/send_emails.php"]}],"glossary":[{"term":"Bug / Issue","meaning":"The tracked work item. Code and tables use 'bug' (bug_api.php, mantis_bug_table); the UI says 'issue'."},{"term":"Bugnote","meaning":"A note or comment on an issue (bugnote_api.php, mantis_bugnote_table)."},{"term":"Access level / threshold","meaning":"Numeric role (VIEWER, REPORTER, UPDATER, DEVELOPER, MANAGER, ADMINISTRATOR); thresholds are config values giving the minimum level for an action."},{"term":"Workflow","meaning":"Allowed status transitions for issues, configured in manage_config_workflow_page.php and core/workflow_api.php."},{"term":"Filter","meaning":"A saved or ad-hoc query over issues (filter_api.php, BugFilterQuery, mantis_filters_table)."},{"term":"Monitor","meaning":"A user who follows an issue and receives notifications (bug_monitor_add.php)."},{"term":"Sponsorship","meaning":"Optional feature where users pledge money on an issue (sponsorship_api.php)."},{"term":"Command","meaning":"Class in core/commands/ that implements one business action, shared by the web UI and the REST API."},{"term":"MantisConnect (mc_)","meaning":"The SOAP API; files in api/soap prefixed mc_. Its ApiObjectFactory is also reused by the REST API."},{"term":"Event / plugin","meaning":"Plugin extension points declared in core/events_inc.php and signalled with event_signal()."},{"term":"g_ / p_ / f_ / c_ / t_ prefixes","meaning":"Variable naming convention from README.md: g_ global config, p_ function parameter, f_ form input, c_ cleaned for DB, t_ temporary."},{"term":"config_inc.php","meaning":"Per-installation configuration file in config/ (gitignored) that overrides config_defaults_inc.php."},{"term":"_page.php / _inc.php","meaning":"Root file naming: *_page.php renders a page, *_inc.php is an include fragment, other root .php files are form action scripts."},{"term":"ADOdb","meaning":"Database abstraction library (adodb/adodb-php) used by core/database_api.php to support MySQL, PostgreSQL and others."},{"term":"Publican / DocBook","meaning":"Toolchain and XML format used to build the Admin Guide and Developers Guide in docbook/."},{"term":"translatewiki.net","meaning":"External site that provides localisation updates to lang/ through automated commits."}]},"stack":{"languages":["PHP (>= 8.1, composer platform 8.1.34)","JavaScript (front-end in js/, Node tooling in tools/)","SQL (via ADOdb)","Shell (CI scripts in build/)","Python (release build scripts in build/)","DocBook XML (docbook/)"],"frameworks":["Slim 3 (REST API)","ADOdb (database abstraction)","PHPMailer (email)","HTMLPurifier and Parsedown (formatting)","Guzzle (HTTP client)","PHPUnit 10.5/11.5 (tests)","Redocly CLI and openapi-to-postmanv2 (OpenAPI tooling)","Bruno and Scalar (API docs tooling in tools/)"],"datastores":["MySQL/MariaDB (mysqli driver, default)","PostgreSQL (pgsql driver, tested in CI)","Other ADOdb-supported databases (README: 'or other supported database')","Local disk for attachments when file_upload_method = DISK"],"external_services":["SMTP / sendmail mail transport (PHPMailer)","LDAP directory (core/ldap_api.php, optional)","Gravatar (plugins/Gravatar)","translatewiki.net (localisation commits)","mantisbt.org issue tracker (where issues are filed, per CONTRIBUTING.md)"]},"architecture":{"components":[{"name":"Web UI pages and actions","kind":"web app","path":"/ (root *.php files), core.php","tech":"PHP server-rendered pages, js/, css/","description":"One PHP file per page (*_page.php) or form action. Each bootstraps core.php, which loads config and connects to the database."},{"name":"Core APIs","kind":"library","path":"core/","tech":"PHP procedural *_api.php modules, core/classes, core/commands, core/exceptions","description":"Business logic: bugs, projects, users, filters, workflow, email, auth, plugins, logging. Commands in core/commands are shared by the UI and the REST API."},{"name":"REST API","kind":"API","path":"api/rest/","tech":"Slim 3, OpenAPI spec in api/rest/mantisbt_openapi.yaml","description":"JSON API with middlewares for auth, cache, offline and version; route files in api/rest/restcore/*_rest.php. Reuses SOAP mc_ code and core commands."},{"name":"SOAP API (MantisConnect)","kind":"API","path":"api/soap/","tech":"PHP SoapServer, WSDL","description":"Legacy SOAP API (mantisconnect.php, mc_*_api.php)."},{"name":"Admin and installer","kind":"web app","path":"admin/","tech":"PHP","description":"Environment checks, install/upgrade (install.php, schema.php, upgrade_unattended.php), email queue and DB stats. Meant to be removed on live sites."},{"name":"Plugins","kind":"extension","path":"plugins/","tech":"PHP, MantisPlugin class, events","description":"Bundled plugins: MantisCoreFormatting, MantisGraph, XmlImportExport, Gravatar. Other plugin folders are gitignored."},{"name":"CLI scripts","kind":"scheduler / worker","path":"scripts/","tech":"PHP CLI","description":"cronjob.php signals EVENT_CRONJOB; send_emails.php sends queued emails when email_send_using_cronjob is on. The cron schedule itself is outside the repository."},{"name":"Database","kind":"database","path":"admin/schema.php","tech":"MySQL or PostgreSQL via ADOdb","description":"Tables prefixed mantis_ (bug, bug_text, bugnote, bug_history, project, project_version, category, user, user_pref, config, filters, tag, plugin, email, api_token, custom_field and more)."},{"name":"Configuration","kind":"config","path":"config_defaults_inc.php, config/config_inc.php.sample","tech":"PHP global $g_ variables","description":"Defaults in config_defaults_inc.php; per-install overrides in config/config_inc.php (gitignored); some settings stored in mantis_config_table."},{"name":"Localisation","kind":"resources","path":"lang/","tech":"PHP string files","description":"66 language files, updated from translatewiki.net."},{"name":"Documentation and API tooling","kind":"build tooling","path":"docbook/, tools/openapi, tools/bruno, tools/scalar, package.json","tech":"DocBook/Publican (Dockerfile in docbook/), Node scripts","description":"Builds the Admin and Developers guides and validates/generates REST API collections and docs."},{"name":"Release build","kind":"build tooling","path":"build/","tech":"Python and shell","description":"buildrelease*.py produce release tarballs; ci_install_mantis.sh and ci_post_install.sh install and seed MantisBT in CI."},{"name":"Mail server","kind":"external service","path":"core/email_api.php, core/classes/EmailSenderPhpMailer.class.php","tech":"PHPMailer (mail, SMTP, sendmail)","description":"Sends notifications; target server is configured per installation."},{"name":"LDAP directory","kind":"external service","path":"core/ldap_api.php","tech":"PHP ldap extension","description":"Optional authentication backend."}],"mermaid":"flowchart LR\n  browser[\"Browser user\"] --> web[\"Web UI pages (root *.php)\"]\n  client[\"API client\"] --> rest[\"REST API (api/rest, Slim)\"]\n  client --> soap[\"SOAP API (api/soap)\"]\n  admin[\"Admin / installer (admin/)\"] --> core\n  web --> core[\"Core APIs and commands (core/)\"]\n  rest --> core\n  rest --> soap\n  soap --> core\n  cron[\"CLI scripts (scripts/)\"] --> core\n  core --> plugins[\"Plugins (plugins/)\"]\n  core --> config[\"Config (config_defaults_inc.php, config/)\"]\n  core --> db[(\"MySQL / PostgreSQL via ADOdb\")]\n  core --> mail[\"Mail server (PHPMailer)\"]\n  core --> ldap[\"LDAP (optional)\"]\n  core --> lang[\"lang/ strings\"]\n  docs[\"Docs tooling (docbook/, tools/)\"] --> spec[\"OpenAPI spec\"]\n  spec --> rest"},"workflows":{"setup":"composer install","run_local":"php -S localhost:8080","test":"vendor/bin/phpunit","lint":"npm run api:validate","build":"npm run api:generate","deploy":null},"requirements":[{"id":"agents-file","status":"fail","evidence":["No AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md at the repository root"],"gap":"There is no agent entry file.","plan":"Create AGENTS.md (under 150 lines) with: what MantisBT is; commands (composer install, npm ci, php -S localhost:8080, vendor/bin/phpunit, npm run api:validate, plus the new check-fast/check scripts); layout (root pages, core/, api/rest, api/soap, admin/, plugins/, lang/, scripts/, tests/, docbook/, build/); conventions from README.md (g_/p_/f_/c_/t_ prefixes, tabs, *_page.php naming) and CONTRIBUTING.md (PR to master, reference a mantisbt.org issue); how tests need an installed instance; what never to do. Add CLAUDE.md containing only '@AGENTS.md'."},{"id":"agents-file-accurate","status":"fail","evidence":["No AGENTS.md to check"],"gap":"Nothing to verify yet.","plan":"Only reference 