ents","status":"pass","evidence":["CONTRIBUTING.md: PRs target master, must reference an issue on mantisbt.org/bugs, follow coding guidelines, rebase to resolve conflicts",".github/pull_request_template.md requires 'Fixes #XXXX'"],"gap":"None for the check. CONTRIBUTING.md has no definition of done that names a local gate.","plan":"nothing (optionally add one short 'Definition of done' line pointing to `composer run check-fast` in CONTRIBUTING.md, without changing existing rules)."},{"id":"task-runner","status":"pass","evidence":["package.json scripts: api:validate, api:generate, api:postman, api:bruno, api:docs","composer.json has no scripts section"],"gap":"The runner only covers OpenAPI tooling; PHP setup, tests and checks have no named task.","plan":"Add a `scripts` section to composer.json (the PHP project's natural runner): setup, test, lint (php -l over core/ api/ admin/ plugins/ scripts/ and root, plus npm run api:validate), check-fast, check, dev. Do not change how the project builds or the existing npm scripts."},{"id":"fast-gate","status":"fail","evidence":["No check-fast target in package.json or composer.json","phpunit.xml: every suite bootstraps core.php via tests/TestConfig.php require_mantis_core(), which needs config/config_inc.php and a reachable database","tests/bootstrap.php (required by phpunit.xml) is not tracked; only tests/bootstrap.php.sample exists"],"gap":"No fast gate, and no existing PHPUnit test can run without an installed MantisBT and database; soap and rest suites also need a running web server.","plan":"Add composer script `check-fast`: PHP syntax lint (php -l over tracked .php files, excluding vendor/), `npm run api:validate`, and `vendor/bin/phpunit --testsuite mantis` against a local database brought up by compose (see local-env). If a DB-free gate is needed, add a small new PHPUnit suite (e.g. tests/Unit) for pure functions that do not call require_mantis_core(). Record in docs/harness/log.md which tests need DB or web server."},{"id":"full-gate","status":"fail","evidence":["No check/verify/ci target",".github/workflows/mantisbt.yml runs composer install, installs MantisBT through build/ci_install_mantis.sh and build/ci_post_install.sh, then vendor/bin/phpunit (all 4 suites)",".github/workflows/documentation.yml runs npm ci, npm run api:validate, npm run api:generate, docbook make"],"gap":"No single command reproduces what CI runs.","plan":"Add composer script `check`: check-fast plus full `vendor/bin/phpunit` (mantis, soap, rest, mantis core formatting suites) against a local install, and `npm run api:generate`. Provide a script (e.g. build/local_install.sh) that reuses build/ci_install_mantis.sh and build/ci_post_install.sh with env vars pointing at the compose database and `php -S localhost:8080`."},{"id":"tests","status":"pass","evidence":["phpunit.xml suites: tests/Mantis, tests/soap, tests/rest, plugins/MantisCoreFormatting/tests","68 test files counted by the deterministic check"],"gap":"Tests exist but all of them are integration tests needing an installed instance and database.","plan":"nothing for the check; document in AGENTS.md how to run one test (`vendor/bin/phpunit --filter StringTest`) and the whole suite, and the install prerequisites."},{"id":"ci","status":"pass","evidence":[".github/workflows/documentation.yml calls npm run api:validate and npm run api:generate on push/pull_request",".github/workflows/mantisbt.yml runs vendor/bin/phpunit on push and pull_request across PHP 8.1-8.5 and mysqli/pgsql"],"gap":"CI does not call a single gate target, so it can drift from what agents run locally.","plan":"After adding composer scripts, make mantisbt.yml call `composer run check` (or keep the matrix steps and replace the final step with the gate). Optionally add a job that runs `npx -y uw-harness verify` with Node 20. Keep the existing matrix, paths-ignore and '[skip ci]' behaviour."},{"id":"hooks","status":"fail","evidence":["No .pre-commit-config.yaml, .husky/, lefthook.yml or .githooks/"],"gap":"No git hooks.","plan":"Add .githooks/pre-push running `composer run check-fast` and set `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` from the composer `setup` script. Keep it non-blocking for contributors without a local DB (document `git push --no-verify` only as a last resort is not acceptable; instead let the hook skip DB tests when tests/bootstrap.php is absent)."},{"id":"local-env","status":"fail","evidence":["No compose file or devcontainer (docbook/Dockerfile only builds docs with Publican)","No dev/start target","CI starts the app with `php -S localhost:8080` and installs via build/ci_install_mantis.sh"],"gap":"No one-command local environment with a database and seed data.","plan":"Add compose.yaml with MySQL (and optionally PostgreSQL) using the CI values (DB bugtracker, user root/root, port mapping). Add composer scripts `dev` (php -S localhost:8080) and `setup` (composer install, npm ci, install hooks, run the installer and seed via build/ci_install_mantis.sh + build/ci_post_install.sh with local env vars, which also writes tests/bootstrap.php). Write docs/local-dev.md: prerequisites (PHP 8.1+ with mysqli/pgsql, mbstring, curl, gd, soap, ldap extensions; Composer; Node; Docker), first run, reset (drop DB, delete config/config_inc.php), debugging (log_level/log_destination, MANTIS_TESTSUITE_XDEBUG_SESSION)."},{"id":"env-example","status":"fail","evidence":["No .env.example; configuration is PHP: config/config_inc.php.sample lists DB, crypto_master_salt, SMTP and email settings with empty or placeholder values","config/ is gitignored, no .env tracked","CI uses env vars HOSTNAME, PORT, DB_NAME, DB_USER, DB_PASSWORD, DB_HOST, DB_TYPE in build/ci_*.sh"],"gap":"The app reads config from PHP files, not env vars; the CI/local install scripts read env vars that are not documented in an example file.","plan":"Add .env.example listing the variables used by build/ci_install_mantis.sh, build/ci_post_install.sh and compose.yaml (HOSTNAME, PORT, DB_TYPE, DB_HOST, DB_NAME, DB_USER, DB_PASSWORD) with safe local values and a comment pointing to config/config_inc.php.sample for application settings. Do not convert the app to env-based config."},{"id":"toolchain-pinned","status":"fail","evidence":["composer.json: require php ^8.1 and config.platform.php 8.1.34 (not counted by the check)","No .nvmrc / .tool-versions / package.json engines","CI matrix tests PHP 8.1 to 8.5; documentation workflow uses runner default Node"],"gap":"Node version is not pinned and no version file exists for PHP.","plan":"Add .tool-versions (or mise.toml) with php 8.1 (the composer platform floor) and node 20, and add `\"engines\": {\"node\": \">=20\"}` to package.json. Do not change composer platform settings."},{"id":"deploy-explicit","status":"partial","evidence":["docbook/Dockerfile builds documentation only, not the application","build/README.md: release process (tag release-x.y.z, buildrelease-repo.py) for tarballs","README.md: install/upgrade by extracting the tarball and running admin/install.php"],"gap":"MantisBT is a distributed product; how releases are published and how mantisbt.org's own instance is deployed is not written in one place.","plan":"Create docs/deploy.md: sections for release build (build/README.md steps, buildrelease-repo.py), installation/upgrade by users (README.md, admin/install.php), branches master and master-X.Y, rollback (restore backup per README), and uw-harness TODO blocks for who can tag and sign releases, where tarballs are published, and how the project's own tracker is upgraded."},{"id":"observability","status":"fail","evidence":["core/logging_api.php: log_event with log_level (default LOG_NONE) and log_destination (file, page, etc.) from config_defaults_inc.php","api/rest/index.php: unhandled errors written with error_log()","admin/check/index.php: environment checks; admin/email_queue.php shows queued emails"],"gap":"No document on logs, errors or health checks.","plan":"Create docs/observability.md describing log_level/log_destination, PHP error_log for REST errors, show_detailed_errors, admin/check as a health check, email queue monitoring, and TODO blocks for where production logs/alerts live for any instance the team runs."},{"id":"skills","status":"fail","evidence":["No .agents/skills/ or .claude/skills/"],"gap":"No playbooks.","plan":"Create .agents/skills/implement-change, debug-local and rest-api-change (edit api/rest/restcore + core/commands + mantisbt_openapi.yaml, then npm run api:validate and the rest test suite), plus add-language-string (lang/strings_english.txt only; other languages come from translatewiki.net). Symlink .claude/skills to .agents/skills. Any deploy skill must link to docs/deploy.md TODOs."}],"questions":[{"requirement":"deploy-explicit","question":"Who can tag and sign a MantisBT release, and where are release tarballs published (SourceForge, GitHub releases, mantisbt.org)?","why":"build/README.md shows the tagging and build commands but not the publishing target or the people allowed to do it."},{"requirement":"deploy-explicit","question":"Is the project's own tracker at mantisbt.org/bugs deployed from this repository, and if so how and by whom is it upgraded?","why":"Nothing in the repository describes a running production instance of this code."},{"requirement":"observability","question":"For any instance the team operates (for example mantisbt.org/bugs), where are PHP error logs and MantisBT logs stored, and is there any alerting?","why":"The code only exposes log_level/log_destination and error_log; locations and alerts are not visible."},{"requirement":"fast-gate","question":"Is it acceptable that the fast gate needs a local database (Docker compose with MySQL), or do you want a separate DB-free unit suite added for the pre-push gate?","why":"Every existing PHPUnit test boots core.php and connects to a database."},{"requirement":"ci","question":"May the harness change .github/workflows/mantisbt.yml to call a composer gate script, or must CI stay as is and only a new workflow be added?","why":"The existing CI is a tuned PHP x DB matrix maintained by the core team."},{"requirement":"agreements","question":"What is the team's definition of done for a pull request beyond CONTRIBUTING.md (passing CI matrix, reviewer count, who merges, rebase or merge commit)?","why":"CONTRIBUTING.md states targeting and rebasing rules but not review or merge rules."},{"requirement":"local-env","question":"Which database should be the default for local development and the harness: MySQL/MariaDB or PostgreSQL?","why":"CI tests both; the default in config_defaults_inc.php is mysqli."}],"risks":["All PHPUnit suites are integration tests: tests/TestConfig.php require_mantis_core() loads core.php, which needs config/config_inc.php and a database; soap and rest suites also need a running web server and an API token (created by tests/ci_create_api_token.php). A naive `vendor/bin/phpunit` on a fresh clone will fail, so the gates will look broken unless setup installs MantisBT first.","phpunit.xml uses bootstrap=tests/bootstrap.php, which is not tracked (only bootstrap.php.sample); build/ci_post_install.sh appends to it. Setup must create it.","phpunit.xml sets failOnAllIssues=true: any PHP deprecation or warning (for example on newer PHP versions) fails the run.","build/check_lineterm.php rewrites files when run with options; do not use it as a read-only lint.","No PHP linter or static analyser is configured (no phpcs, phpstan, php-cs-fixer); a lint gate must be added from scratch (php -l is the safe minimum).","Very large legacy procedural codebase (82 entries in core/, ~200 root PHP pages, global $g_ variables) with 15,000+ commits; changes can have wide side effects not covered by tests.","dapphp/securimage is pulled from a VCS repository (github.com/mantisbt/securimage, no-api), so composer install needs network access to GitHub.","Localisation files in lang/ (except English) are overwritten by translatewiki.net commits; agents editing them directly will have changes lost.","admin/ is meant to be removed on live sites; harness scripts must not assume it is reachable in production.","CI is skipped on commits containing '[skip ci]' (translatewiki commits), so those changes are never tested."],"notes_for_apply":"Runtime: PHP 8.1+ (composer platform pinned to 8.1.34; CI tests 8.1-8.5, 8.6 experimental) with extensions mysqli, pgsql, mbstring, json, tokenizer, curl, gd, fileinfo, ldap, soap, zlib (from mantisbt.yml), plus ext-zip for dev. Node 20 for package.json tooling (npm ci). Install with `composer install` (needs GitHub access for dapphp/securimage) and `npm ci`.\n\nReuse composer.json as the PHP task runner by adding a `scripts` section (setup, dev, test, lint, check-fast, check); keep the existing npm api:* scripts untouched. No Makefile exists; do not add one unless composer scripts prove insufficient.\n\nTo run tests locally, mirror CI: start a DB (add compose.yaml with MySQL root/root, database bugtracker), run `php -S localhost:8080` from the repo root, `chmod 777 config/`, then run build/ci_install_mantis.sh and build/ci_post_install.sh with HOSTNAME, PORT, DB_TYPE, DB_HOST, DB_NAME, DB_USER, DB_PASSWORD exported and DB_CMD set (the CI step defines DB_CMD; local scripts must set it too, e.g. `mysql -h127.0.0.1 -uroot -proot bugtracker -e`). ci_post_install.sh uses `sudo chmod` and appends to tests/bootstrap.php and config/config_inc.php, so it is not idempotent: a reset must drop the DB and delete those two files. Prefer a new wrapper script under build/ rather than editing the CI scripts.\n\nNo test is known to be broken on the current code (CI badge on master), but none can run without the installed instance. Suites: mantis, soap, rest, 'mantis core formatting' (use `--testsuite mantis` for a quicker run). failOnAllIssues=true makes deprecations fatal.\n\nDo not touch: vendor/ (composer), lang/ files other than strings_english.txt (translatewiki.net), config_defaults_inc.php semantics, the CI matrix behaviour, docbook build. Do not run build/check_lineterm.php in a gate (it rewrites files). Commit style: short imperative subject lines ('Fix tag cache invalidation', 'Test ... ', 'GHA: ...'); PRs target master and must reference a mantisbt.org issue. Writing rules for prose: no em-dashes, simple English, no hard-wrapping."}}}
